      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/w0xlt/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "An empty `addnode=` entry currently creates an empty added-node record. The node then repeatedly attempts to connect to the empty destination:\r\n\r\n```text\r\n2026-07-23T19:22:33Z [net] trying v2 connection (manual) to , lastseen=0.0hrs\r\n2026-07-23T19:23:33Z [net] trying v2 connection (manual) to , lastseen=0.0hrs\r\n2026-07-23T19:24:34Z [net] trying v2 connection (manual) to , lastseen=0.0hrs\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this change, the node ignores empty `-addnode` values when initializing the connection manager. This preserves the existing startup behavior while avoiding useless connection attempts. Non-empty values are unaffected.\r\n\r\nA functional test verifies that the node starts with `addnode=` and that no added-node record is created.",
